{"name":"Tear","hex":"#b5d8df","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tear","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To rend (a solid material) by holding or restraining in two places and pulling apart, whether intentionally or not; to destroy or separate.","To injure as if by pulling apart."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hole or break caused by tearing.","A rampage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tear"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tearing (physics)","blocks":[{"text":"Tearing is the act of breaking apart a material by force, without the aid of a cutting tool. A tear in a piece of paper, fabric, or some other similar object may be the result of the intentional effort with one's bare hands, or be accidental. Unlike a cut, which is generally on a straight or patterned line controlled by a tool such as scissors, a tear is generally uneven and, for the most part, unplanned. An exception is a tear along a perforated line, as found on a roll of toilet paper or paper towels, which has been previously partially cut, so the effort of tearing will probably produce a straight line."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/dd/Tornpaper.jpg/330px-Tornpaper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tearing_(physics)"},{"title":"Tears","blocks":[{"text":"Tears are a transparent fluid secreted primarily by the lacrimal glands found in the eyes of all land mammals. According to the mode of production, tears are classified into four types: basal, closed eye, emotional, and reflex. The basal rate of tear secretion is ~0.5–2.2 μL/min, and irritation can increase secretion by up to ~100-fold, reaching ~300 μL/min. Tears are made up of water, electrolytes, proteins, lipids, and mucins that form layers on the surface of eyes. The four types of tears differ significantly in their composition."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/USMC-04952.jpg/330px-USMC-04952.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tears"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Mending_the_Tears_LACMA_54.86.5.jpg/500px-Mending_the_Tears_LACMA_54.86.5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Mending_the_Tears_LACMA_54.86.5.jpg/1280px-Mending_the_Tears_LACMA_54.86.5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Mending_the_Tears_LACMA_54.86.5.jpg/500px-Mending_the_Tears_LACMA_54.86.5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mending the Tears, print by Winslow Homer  (1888), Los Angeles County Museum of Art ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMending_the_Tears_LACMA_54.86.5.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crying-girl.jpg/500px-Crying-girl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crying-girl.jpg/1280px-Crying-girl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crying-girl.jpg/500px-Crying-girl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A toddler producing tears due to emotional stress or pain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrying-girl.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Crying_boy.jpg/500px-Crying_boy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Crying_boy.jpg/500px-Crying_boy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crying boy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrying_boy.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/D._Maria_II_%28BM_1868%2C0612.2285%29.jpg/500px-D._Maria_II_%28BM_1868%2C0612.2285%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/D._Maria_II_%28BM_1868%2C0612.2285%29.jpg/1280px-D._Maria_II_%28BM_1868%2C0612.2285%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/D._Maria_II_%28BM_1868%2C0612.2285%29.jpg/500px-D._Maria_II_%28BM_1868%2C0612.2285%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Queen Maria II of Portugal shedding tears and hugging a bust of her late father King Pedro IV (also Emperor of Brazil as Pedro I), 1836","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AD._Maria_II_(BM_1868%2C0612.2285).jpg"}],"sounds":{"tear":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b2/En-us-tear-verb.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b2/En-us-tear-verb.ogg/En-us-tear-verb.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/88/En-us-tear-noun.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/88/En-us-tear-noun.ogg/En-us-tear-noun.ogg.mp3"}]}}}